f one side. In the input, the nub's side of the bounding box contains exactly one cell. The other three sides are full frame edges.\n\n**What the output adds.** Each object gets a mirrored copy on the side opposite its nub, with a one-cell gap from the frame.\n\n- Pair 1, top-left object (rows 3–7, nub on top at row 3): an 8-coloured copy appears in rows 9–13. Its frame is in rows 9–12 and its nub now points down at row 13. That is the object flipped top-to-bottom and moved down by its height + 1 (5 + 1 = 6).\n- Pair 1, object at cols 10–14 (nub on the right at col 14): a 1-coloured copy appears at cols 4–8 with its nub on the left at col 4. It is flipped left-to-right and moved left by width + 1.\n- Pair 1, small object at cols 11–14 (nub on the left): its copy should span cols 16–19. Col 19 is off the grid, so only the frame (cols 16–18) shows. Copies are therefore clipped at the border.\n- Pairs 2 and 3 follow the same pattern. Nubs pointing left or right give a horizontal copy in colour 1. Nubs pointing up or down give a vertical copy in colour 8. The offset is always bbox size + 1, away from the nub.\n\n**Rule.**\n1. For each object, find the bbox edge (top, bottom, left or right) that contains exactly one cell. That edge is the nub side.\n2. Flip the object along that axis.\n3. Shift the flipped object by (bbox extent + 1) in the direction opposite the nub.\n4. Paint it 8 for a vertical flip or 1 for a horizontal flip, clipping at the grid border.\n\n**Test.** Four objects:\n- Nub left at row 6 → copy to the right in colour 1.\n- Nub right → copy to the left in colour 1.\n- Nub bottom → copy above in colour 8.\n- Small one with nub on top → copy below in colour 8.\n\nNone of these copies leaves the grid.","code":"def transform(grid):\n    g = np.array(grid)\n    bg = background(g)\n    out = g.copy()\n    H, W = g.shape\n    for o in objects(g, bg=bg):\n        y0, x0, y1, x1 = o[\"box\"]\n        m = (o[\"grid\"] != bg)\n        h, w = m.shape\n        sides = {\"top\": m[0].sum(), \"bottom\": m[-1].sum(),\n                 \"left\": m[:, 0].sum(), \"right\": m[:, -1].sum()}\n        nub = [k for k, v in sides.items() if v == 1]\n        if not nub:\n            continue\n        nub = nub[0]\n        if nub == \"top\":\n            pat, dy, dx, col = m[::-1], h + 1, 0, 8\n        elif nub == \"bottom\":\n            pat, dy, dx, col = m[::-1], -(h + 1), 0, 8\n        elif nub == \"left\":\n            pat, dy, dx, col = m[:, ::-1], 0, w + 1, 1\n        else:\n            pat, dy, dx, col = m[:, ::-1], 0, -(w + 1), 1\n        for yy in range(h):\n            for xx in range(w):\n                if pat[yy, xx]:\n                    ty, tx = y0 + dy + yy, x0 + dx + xx\n                    if 0 <= ty < H and 0 <= tx < W:\n                        out[ty, tx] = col\n        emit(out, f\"Mirrored object at {o['box']} away from its {nub} nub, painted colour {col}\")\n    emit(out, \"Final grid\")\n    return out\n","candidate_tactics":{"rigid":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"**What the output adds.** Each object gets a mirrored copy on the side opposite its nub, with a one-cell gap from the frame."},{"source":"verified program checkpoint","text":"Mirrored object at (2, 11, 4, 14) away from its left nub, painted colour 1"},{"source":"verified program checkpoint","text":"Mirrored object at (3, 3, 7, 7) away from its top nub, painted colour 8"}],"movement":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"Shift the flipped object by (bbox extent + 1) in the direction opposite the nub."}],"crop":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"In the input, the nub's side of the bounding box contains exactly one cell."}],"layers":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"- Pair 1, top-left object (rows 3–7, nub on top at row 3): an 8-coloured copy appears in rows 9–13."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"- Small one with nub on top → copy below in colour 8."}]},"provenance":{"reference_assisted":false,"query_labels_used_for_rule_diagnosis":false},"artifact_sha256":"12cf5df538646cbcd1149a6183b56be44e68b422856ddb526c5a282f9e601b3a","task_sha256":"146638a6ba67909b27d289f5debc9ab044e4bc5626be826bf33cd854cd1ec1e9","validation":"Frozen corpus recorded successful replay on teaching fixtures; synthetic generalization not established."}
